    {
      "block_id": 18,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "If sprite DMA is turned off while a sprite is being displayed (that is, after VSTART \nbut before VSTOP), the system will continue to display the line of sprite data that was \nmost recently fetched. This causes a vertical bar to appear on the screen. It is recom­\nmended that sprite DMA be turned off only during vertical blanking or during some \nportion of the display where you are sure that no sprite is being displayed.\n",
